    "https://careers.usc.edu.au/jobs/payroll-officer-unisc-moreton-bay-queensland-australia": {
      "title": "Payroll Officer",
      "description": "Payroll Officer - UniSC Moreton Bay, Queensland, Australia Contact Us Candidate login Explore Opportunities Academic jobs Professional jobs Casual jobs Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander jobs Recruitment process Employer information Applicant Settings Kiosk mode < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNITIES Payroll Officer 1 Moreton Parade, UniSC Moreton Bay, Queensland, Australia, 4502 Administration / Admin Support L5 $82,843 - $93,358 +17% super People and Culture Professional Show More Show Less Full-Time Add to favourites View favourites People and Culture | UniSC Moreton Bay, Petrie Level 5, $82,843 - $93,358 p.a., plus up to 17% employer superannuation Full-time, Ongoing appointment The Opportunity At UniSC, our People and Culture team is dedicated to creating an exceptional employee experience that enables our people to thrive. As a Payroll Officer, you will play a key role in ensuring every staff member is paid accurately, on time, and in accordance with legislative and University requirements. Supporting the delivery of the University's fortnightly payroll, you will provide trusted advice on payroll, superannuation, taxation, and employment conditions while maintaining compliance with complex industrial instruments and legislative obligations. Your expertise and attention to detail will contribute to the integrity of our payroll operations and the continuous improvement of systems and processes that enhance service delivery. Working within a collaborative and customer-focused team, you will build positive relationships with colleagues across the University, delivering responsive, high-quality payroll support and helping to ensure a seamless experience for our people. You will Provision of advice on a broad range of payroll and superannuation matters; Contribute to the efficient and effective delivery of the University’s fortnightly payroll functions; and Ensure compliance with relevant legislation, policy and procedures. About you You are a detail-oriented payroll professional who thrives on accuracy, compliance, and delivering exceptional service. With a strong understanding of payroll legislation, industrial instruments, and employment conditions, you enjoy working in a fast-paced environment where precision and deadlines matter. You confidently provide trusted advice, build positive relationships across a diverse organisation, and apply your analytical and problem-solving skills to resolve complex payroll matters, identify opportunities for process improvement, and contribute to the continuous enhancement of payroll services. You will possess: Extensive experience in the accurate preparation and completion of fortnightly payroll processes within a large organisation, including demonstrated knowledge of superannuation and taxation legislation; Strong analytical skills with expertise in structured and ad hoc reporting, and proficiency in the use of a complex HRIS, preferably PeopleSoft; Experience providing accurate advice and dealing with enquiries involving interpreting employment conditions, policies, procedures and guidelines while providing quality customer service; The capacity to exercise sound judgement, take initiative and solve problems, as required; Excellent computing and word processing skills with high-level experience in the development and maintenance of databases and spreadsheets; and High level organisational and interpersonal skills including the ability to communicate effectively both verbally and in writing. Don't meet every requirement? At UniSC, we understand that your work and life experiences can be just as valuable. If you're excited about this role but your CV doesn't align perfectly with our position description, we encourage you to apply anyway. You may be just the right candidate for this or one of our many other opportunities. UniSC is an equal opportunity employer, committed to diversity and inclusion. We encourage applications from all backgrounds, including those with disabilities, women in STEM, First Nations Peoples, and individuals of diverse cultures, genders, abilities, and experiences. We value achievement relative to opportunity and encourage your commentary on your achievements in this context. For additional support during the application process, please contact us at unisc-careers@usc.edu.au or call +61 7 5430 2830. How to apply All applications must be lodged through our website. To apply please visit our website at: Careers at UniSC We will be reviewing applications and contacting suitable candidates throughout the duration of this advertisement. We strongly encourage you to submit your interest as soon as possible. Position description: 494704_Payroll Officer.pdf Your completed application must include: a resume and a statement of suitability (not to exceed two pages) , which will be reviewed in alignment to the specified selection criteria as outlined within the position description. Further information regarding how to prepare your application is available on our website: Join our team. Have questions or want to know more? For a confidential discussion, please contact: Emma Bayles Associate Director, Employee Experience – People and Culture Telephone: 07 5459 4492 Email: ebayles@usc.edu.au We would love the opportunity to get to know you better, but we know it works both ways. To get to know a little more about us, visit us at: Welcome to UniSC and LinkedIn Life UniSC values a diverse and talented workforce and invites applications from candidates who already have legal work rights in Australia. UniSC does not accept unsolicited applications. For agency inquiries, contact unisc-careers@usc.edu.au Discover UniSC We’re all about doing work that matters, connecting with great people, and being part of an incredible journey. While we’re not the largest university, we are one of the fastest growing in Australia, now with over 2,000 staff across five campuses in South East Queensland and an expanding presence in major capital cities, and we’re making a big impact every day through ground-breaking research, a strong commitment to sustainability, high-performance sport, and award-winning alumni. We are committed to delivering high-quality research and teaching that address major global and regional challenges, with established and emerging strengths in sustainability, environmental systems, biodiversity, aquaculture, preventative health and regional resilience. Our research excellence is internationally recognised through strong performance in global benchmarking, including leading rankings in the 2025 Times Higher Education (THE) Impact Rankings for “Zero Hunger,” “Climate Action” and “Life on Land.” UniSC is also recognised for its teaching excellence, with a strong emphasis on student success, innovative and engaging learning experiences, and strong graduate outcomes that equip learners to make meaningful contributions in their chosen fields. As the only university operating within three UNESCO Biosphere Reserves and a UNESCO World Heritage Site, UniSC is uniquely positioned to leverage its natural environment to advance impactful research, teaching and partnerships that support sustainable futures, with sustainability embedded across all aspects of our teaching, research and operations. We foster a collaborative and supportive environment that encourages continuous professional development and provides the tools and resources to grow your career. We value the contributions of every team member and the role they play in our culture and success. We’re not afraid to do things differently, and we’re looking for people who share our values and want to be part of a team working together to make a meaningful difference to local and global challenges. Our Culture & Benefits: Our collaborative, passionate and welcoming culture is what really sets us apart. Modern teaching & research facilities. Professional development and career pathway opportunities. We are a proud recipient of the prestigious Athena SWAN Bronze Award, granted as part of the Science in Australia Gender Equity (SAGE) initiative. Flexible work arrangements & generous leave options. Salary packing options + 17% Super. EAP, fitness passport & discounted private health. Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 0:00 Loaded : 0% Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 0:00 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles subtitles settings , opens subtitles settings dialog subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNTIES Apply now! Enter your details below to commence your application: First Name (required) c7c001c5 Last Name (required) 997f9594 Email (required) d4f3413e Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you About UniSC For more information about UniSC's employment benefits and culture, including employee blogs, visit our employer information page . Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 0:00 Loaded : 0% Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 0:00 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles subtitles settings , opens subtitles settings dialog subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. Recommended for you Clinical Trial Associate UniSC SouthBank Clinical Trials, Individual contributor, L5 $82,843 - $93,358 +17% super, Professional Join UniSC's SouthBank clinic to support compliant, high-quality research, ensuring ethical protocols, Good Clinical Practice standards, and impactful outcomes are met. Administration Officer (Program Support) UniSC Sunshine Coast Academic Support Unit, Administration / Admin Support, L5 $82,843 - $93,358 +17% super Join UniSC and play an important role in supporting high-quality learning and research experiences for Honours and HDR students. Senior Clinical Trial Coordinator UniSC Sunshine Coast Clinical Trials, Individual contributor, L7 $105,843 - $115,703 +17% super, Nursing, Professional Join UniSC and lead clinical trial teams to deliver high-quality, ICH/GCP-compliant research, using expert coordination, problem-solving and innovative approaches to drive successful trial outcomes. Change Manager - Timetabling UniSC Sunshine Coast Individual contributor, Information Technology, L8 $118,986 - $134,756 +17% super Join UniSC’s PACE transformation and lead organisational change for a major evolution of the University’s timetabling and learning and teaching environment, helping staff and stakeholders successfully navigate and embrace new ways of working. Join our talent community! Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 0fb17e6e Last Name (required) e9c766f6 Email (required) cf622ec5 Job Alert efd511f5 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Administration / Admin Support L5 $82,843 - $93,358 +17% super People and Culture Professional Administration / Admin Support L5 $82,843 - $93,358 +17% super People and Culture Professional Employment Type Full-Time Full-Time Locations UniSC Moreton Bay, Queensland, Australia UniSC Moreton Bay, Queensland, Australia Send Please wait... Done Not You? Congratulations from the UniSC Talent Acquisition Team, you are now signed up for UniSC job alerts. Apply now! Enter your details below to commence your application: First Name (required) d07ba49c Last Name (required) 15413145 Email (required) 0ca70939 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 0:00 Loaded : 0% Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 0:00 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles subtitles settings , opens subtitles settings dialog subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. LEGAL Privacy Copyright Disclaimer Right to Information Data Collection Preferences The University of the Sunshine Coast acknowledges the Traditional Custodians of the land on which we live, work and study. We pay our respects to local Indigenous Elders past, present and emerging and recognise the strength, resilience and capacity of all Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people. ABN 28 441 859 157 | CRICOS Provider No. 01595D | TEQSA Provider No. PRV12082 Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. By continuing, you agree that you have read our Privacy Statement I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
