    "https://careers.usc.edu.au/jobs/change-manager-timetabling-unisc-sunshine-coast-qld-australia": {
      "title": "Change Manager",
      "description": "Change Manager - Timetabling - UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia Contact Us Candidate login Explore Opportunities Academic jobs Professional jobs Casual jobs Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander jobs Recruitment process Employer information Applicant Settings Kiosk mode < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNITIES Change Manager - Timetabling 90 Sippy Downs Drive, UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia, 4556 Individual contributor Information Technology L8 $118,986 - $134,756 +17% super Full-Time Add to favourites View favourites Information Technology Services | UniSC Sunshine Coast, Sippy Downs Level 8, $118,986 - $134,756 p.a., plus up to 17% employer superannuation Full-time (36.25 hrs per week), fixed term appointment for 12 months The Opportunity UniSC’s PACE Learning and Teaching Model is a major University-wide transformation designed to enhance the student learning experience and support contemporary approaches to teaching and learning. Its implementation is creating new opportunities to improve how students, academics and professional staff engage with learning, teaching and timetabling, supported by new processes, systems and ways of working. As the Change Manager, Timetabling, you will lead organisational change and communication activities to support the successful adoption of new timetabling processes and ways of working across the University. Working closely with project teams and stakeholders, you will assess impacts and readiness, manage resistance, build stakeholder confidence and ensure change is effectively embedded, providing senior change management expertise across a complex, University-wide transformation For more information, please visit us online: Information Technology You will lead the planning and delivery of change management and communication activities across the project lifecycle to support successful adoption of new timetabling processes and ways of working; build strong relationships with stakeholders across the University, conducting impact and readiness assessments, identifying resistance and developing strategies to support effective change adoption; and provide expert change management advice across projects, managing risks and quality while contributing to the continuous improvement of change management frameworks, practices and organisational capability. About you You are an experienced change management professional with a strong track record of leading organisational change within complex environments. You bring a practical and people-focused approach to transformation, with the ability to understand business impacts, build readiness and support stakeholders through significant change. A confident and collaborative relationship builder, you can influence stakeholders at all levels and navigate complex environments with empathy, diplomacy and sound business judgement. You are skilled at translating change objectives into practical strategies that engage people, manage resistance and support successful adoption. You will possess: Postgraduate qualifications in organisational change, project management, communications or a related discipline, together with extensive relevant experience; or an equivalent combination of extensive experience and expertise; Extensive knowledge of contemporary organisational change management approaches and demonstrated experience applying them within complex service environments; Significant experience leading change and transformation initiatives, including change impact and readiness assessments, stakeholder engagement and adoption strategies; Demonstrated experience developing and delivering communication, change management and training activities that support business transformation and successful adoption of change; Excellent business acumen, relationship management and facilitation skills, with the ability to influence stakeholders, identify impacts, manage resistance and build readiness for change; and Highly developed communication and interpersonal skills, including the ability to exercise confidentiality, diplomacy, active listening, empathy and respect when working with diverse stakeholders and teams. Don't meet every requirement? At UniSC, we understand that your work and life experiences can be just as valuable. If you're excited about this role but your CV doesn't align perfectly with our position description, we encourage you to apply anyway. You may be just the right candidate for this or one of our many other opportunities. UniSC is an equal opportunity employer, committed to diversity and inclusion. We encourage applications from all backgrounds, including those with disabilities, women in STEM, First Nations Peoples, and individuals of diverse cultures, genders, abilities, and experiences. We value achievement relative to opportunity and encourage your commentary on your achievements in this context. For additional support during the application process, please contact us at unisc-careers@usc.edu.au or call +61 7 5430 2830. How to apply Applications for this position close midnight, Sunday 20 September 2026. Position Description: 494700_Change Manager - Timetabling.pdf Your completed application must include: a resume and a statement of suitability (not to exceed two pages), which will be reviewed in alignment to the specified selection criteria as outlined within the position description. All applications must be lodged through our website. To apply please visit our website at: Careers at UniSC Further information regarding how to prepare your application is available on our website: Join our team. Have questions or want to know more? For a confidential discussion, please contact: Nico Bekker Manager, Program Delivery - IT - Engagemnt & Transfrm Serv- IT Email: nbekker@unisc.edu.au We would love the opportunity to get to know you better, but we know it works both ways. To get to know a little more about us, visit us at: Welcome to UniSC and LinkedIn Life UniSC values a diverse and talented workforce and invites applications from candidates who already have legal work rights in Australia. UniSC does not accept unsolicited applications. For agency inquiries, contact unisc-careers@usc.edu.au Discover UniSC We’re all about doing work that matters, connecting with great people, and being part of an incredible journey. While we’re not the largest university, we are one of the fastest growing in Australia, now with over 2,000 staff across five campuses in South East Queensland and an expanding presence in major capital cities, and we’re making a big impact every day through ground-breaking research, a strong commitment to sustainability, high-performance sport, and award-winning alumni. We are committed to delivering high-quality research and teaching that address major global and regional challenges, with established and emerging strengths in sustainability, environmental systems, biodiversity, aquaculture, preventative health and regional resilience. Our research excellence is internationally recognised through strong performance in global benchmarking, including leading rankings in the 2025 Times Higher Education (THE) Impact Rankings for “Zero Hunger,” “Climate Action” and “Life on Land.” UniSC is also recognised for its teaching excellence, with a strong emphasis on student success, innovative and engaging learning experiences, and strong graduate outcomes that equip learners to make meaningful contributions in their chosen fields. As the only university operating within three UNESCO Biosphere Reserves and a UNESCO World Heritage Site, UniSC is uniquely positioned to leverage its natural environment to advance impactful research, teaching and partnerships that support sustainable futures, with sustainability embedded across all aspects of our teaching, research and operations. We foster a collaborative and supportive environment that encourages continuous professional development and provides the tools and resources to grow your career. We value the contributions of every team member and the role they play in our culture and success. We’re not afraid to do things differently, and we’re looking for people who share our values and want to be part of a team working together to make a meaningful difference to local and global challenges. Our Culture & Benefits: Our collaborative, passionate and welcoming culture is what really sets us apart. Modern teaching & research facilities. Professional development and career pathway opportunities. We are a proud recipient of the prestigious Athena SWAN Bronze Award, granted as part of the Science in Australia Gender Equity (SAGE) initiative. Flexible work arrangements & generous leave options. Salary packing options + 17% Super. EAP, fitness passport & discounted private health. Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 0:00 Loaded : 0% Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 0:00 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles subtitles settings , opens subtitles settings dialog subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNTIES About UniSC For more information about UniSC's employment benefits and culture, including employee blogs, visit our employer information page . Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 0:00 Loaded : 0% Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 0:00 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles subtitles settings , opens subtitles settings dialog subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. Recommended for you Clinical Trial Associate UniSC SouthBank Clinical Trials, Individual contributor, L5 $82,843 - $93,358 +17% super, Professional Join UniSC's SouthBank clinic to support compliant, high-quality research, ensuring ethical protocols, Good Clinical Practice standards, and impactful outcomes are met. Administration Officer (Program Support) UniSC Sunshine Coast Academic Support Unit, Administration / Admin Support, L5 $82,843 - $93,358 +17% super Join UniSC and play an important role in supporting high-quality learning and research experiences for Honours and HDR students. Senior Clinical Trial Coordinator UniSC Sunshine Coast Clinical Trials, Individual contributor, L7 $105,843 - $115,703 +17% super, Nursing, Professional Join UniSC and lead clinical trial teams to deliver high-quality, ICH/GCP-compliant research, using expert coordination, problem-solving and innovative approaches to drive successful trial outcomes. Manager, Organisational Change and Benefits Realisation UniSC Sunshine Coast Enterprise Portfolio and Delivery Office, L9 $138,698 - $145,268 +17% super, Professional Reporting to the Director, Enterprise Portfolio and Delivery, you will lead the development and continuous improvement of UniSC's organisational change and benefits realisation capability. Apply now! Enter your details below to commence your application: First Name (required) 1fc0fc22 Last Name (required) 3ec8bfe2 Email (required) 0368f508 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 0:00 Loaded : 0% Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 0:00 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles subtitles settings , opens subtitles settings dialog subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. LEGAL Privacy Copyright Disclaimer Right to Information Data Collection Preferences The University of the Sunshine Coast acknowledges the Traditional Custodians of the land on which we live, work and study. We pay our respects to local Indigenous Elders past, present and emerging and recognise the strength, resilience and capacity of all Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people. ABN 28 441 859 157 | CRICOS Provider No. 01595D | TEQSA Provider No. PRV12082 Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. By continuing, you agree that you have read our Privacy Statement I do not accept I accept"
