    "https://careers.usc.edu.au/jobs/expression-of-interest-gps-other-qualified-medical-practitioners-unisc-sunshine-coast-qld-australia": {
      "title": "Expression of Interest: GPs & other Qualified Medical Practitioners",
      "description": "Expression of Interest: GPs & other Qualified Medical Practitioners - UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia Contact Us Candidate login Explore Opportunities Academic jobs Professional jobs Casual jobs Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander jobs Recruitment process Employer information Applicant Settings Kiosk mode < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNITIES Expression of Interest: GPs & other Qualified Medical Practitioners 90 Sippy Downs Drive, UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia, 4556 Casual Professional Clinical Trials Professional Casual Add to favourites View favourites UniSC Clinical Trials Medical Practitioners UniSC Clinical Trials is inviting expressions of interest  from qualified medical practitioners to join Queensland’s fastest growing network of clinical research professionals across our Sunshine Coast and Morayfield locations. This expression of interest will support current and future opportunities across our expanding portfolio of clinical trials, delivered through a university-backed, globally connected research environment. If you are interested in contributing to innovative healthcare while maintaining flexibility in your clinical career, we welcome your application. About UniSC Clinical Trials UniSC Clinical Trials is one of South-East Queensland’s leading clinical research networks, delivering Phase I–IV trials across a diverse range of therapeutic areas. Supported by dedicated project, regulatory and nursing teams, our investigators work within a high-quality, GCP-compliant environment with strong governance, established primarily international sponsor relationships, and an active pipeline of studies. Our sites span South-East Queensland across Brisbane, Moreton Bay and Sunshine Coast regions with opportunities for flexible scheduling and multiple work locations with continued growth across priority therapeutic areas. About the expression of interest Applications received through this EOI will be  considered for a range of clinician opportunities including: Principal Investigator (PI) roles Sub-Investigator roles Expert Advisor and Patient Referrals While appointments are typically sessional and designed to complement existing clinical practice, the volume of research activity may support full-time involvement for interested clinicians. What we’re looking for We are seeking clinicians who: Are registered medical practitioners in Australia Have an interest in clinical research and advancing evidence-based medicine Demonstrate strong patient care, professionalism, and ethical standards Are interested in flexible, portfolio-based career opportunities Clinicians will be engaged as independent contractors, and must meet the associated contractor requirements, including holding (or being willing to obtain) an Australian Business Number (ABN) and meeting any applicable insurance, compliance, and associated requirements. Previous clinical trial experience not essential. Training, support and mentoring will be provided. Why join UniSC Clinical Trials Flexible, sessional engagement models Opportunity to contribute to globally sponsored research Strong operational and regulatory support Access to multidisciplinary research teams Professional development in clinical research How to apply Your expression of interest must be submitted online, and include: A short statement outlining your interest in clinical research, including any research experience or areas of interest A brief summary of your clinical background, specialty, and/or r esume Preferred work location(s) Applications will be retained in our talent pool and reviewed as opportunities become available. Contact For further information about this opportunity, please contact: Lucas Litewka, Director, UniSC Clinical Trials Centre Phone: +617 5456 5265 Email: llitewka@usc.edu.au OR Jessica Baird, Deputy Director, UniSC Clinical Trials Phone: +61754563556 Email: jbaird@usc.edu.au Join us Be part of a collaborative research environment contributing to the future of healthcare, locally and globally. Discover UniSC We’re all about doing work that matters, connecting with great people, and being part of an incredible journey. While we’re not the largest university, we are one of the fastest growing in Australia, now with over 2,000 staff across five campuses in South East Queensland and an expanding presence in major capital cities, and we’re making a big impact every day through ground-breaking research, a strong commitment to sustainability, high-performance sport, and award-winning alumni. We are committed to delivering high-quality research and teaching that address major global and regional challenges, with established and emerging strengths in sustainability, environmental systems, biodiversity, aquaculture, preventative health and regional resilience. Our research excellence is internationally recognised through strong performance in global benchmarking, including leading rankings in the 2025 Times Higher Education (THE) Impact Rankings for “Zero Hunger,” “Climate Action” and “Life on Land.” UniSC is also recognised for its teaching excellence, with a strong emphasis on student success, innovative and engaging learning experiences, and strong graduate outcomes that equip learners to make meaningful contributions in their chosen fields. As the only university operating within three UNESCO Biosphere Reserves and a UNESCO World Heritage Site, UniSC is uniquely positioned to leverage its natural environment to advance impactful research, teaching and partnerships that support sustainable futures, with sustainability embedded across all aspects of our teaching, research and operations. We foster a collaborative and supportive environment that encourages continuous professional development and provides the tools and resources to grow your career. We value the contributions of every team member and the role they play in our culture and success. We’re not afraid to do things differently, and we’re looking for people who share our values and want to be part of a team working together to make a meaningful difference to local and global challenges. < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNTIES Apply now! Enter your details below to commence your application: First Name (required) 1322564a Last Name (required) 6aa88306 Email (required) 2dd8b408 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you About UniSC For more information about UniSC's employment benefits and culture, including employee blogs, visit our employer information page . Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 3:17 Loaded : 0% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 3:17 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles subtitles settings , opens subtitles settings dialog subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. Recommended for you Clinical Trial Associate UniSC SouthBank Clinical Trials, Individual contributor, L5 $82,843 - $93,358 +17% super, Professional Join UniSC's SouthBank clinic to support compliant, high-quality research, ensuring ethical protocols, Good Clinical Practice standards, and impactful outcomes are met. Administration Officer (Program Support) UniSC Sunshine Coast Academic Support Unit, Administration / Admin Support, L5 $82,843 - $93,358 +17% super Join UniSC and play an important role in supporting high-quality learning and research experiences for Honours and HDR students. Senior Clinical Trial Coordinator UniSC Sunshine Coast Clinical Trials, Individual contributor, L7 $105,843 - $115,703 +17% super, Nursing, Professional Join UniSC and lead clinical trial teams to deliver high-quality, ICH/GCP-compliant research, using expert coordination, problem-solving and innovative approaches to drive successful trial outcomes. Change Manager - Timetabling UniSC Sunshine Coast Individual contributor, Information Technology, L8 $118,986 - $134,756 +17% super Join UniSC’s PACE transformation and lead organisational change for a major evolution of the University’s timetabling and learning and teaching environment, helping staff and stakeholders successfully navigate and embrace new ways of working. Join our talent community! Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 931f60ce Last Name (required) ba0e4e08 Email (required) 7f9eac0f Job Alert f9af5804 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Casual Professional Clinical Trials Professional Casual Professional Clinical Trials Professional Employment Type Casual Casual Locations UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia Send Please wait... Done Not You? Congratulations from the UniSC Talent Acquisition Team, you are now signed up for UniSC job alerts. Apply now! Enter your details below to commence your application: First Name (required) e349a65c Last Name (required) 91cdc19b Email (required) 0ca98ed4 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute 