    "https://careers.usc.edu.au/jobs/manager-organisational-change-and-benefits-realisation-unisc-sunshine-coast-qld-australia": {
      "title": "Manager, Organisational Change and Benefits Realisation",
      "description": "Manager, Organisational Change and Benefits Realisation - UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia Contact Us Candidate login Explore Opportunities Academic jobs Professional jobs Casual jobs Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander jobs Recruitment process Employer information Applicant Settings Kiosk mode < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNITIES Manager, Organisational Change and Benefits Realisation 90 Sippy Downs Drive, UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia, 4556 Enterprise Portfolio and Delivery Office L9 $138,698 - $145,268 +17% super Professional Full-Time Add to favourites View favourites Enterprise Portfolio and Delivery Office, Sunshine Coast Campus, Sippy Downs Level 9, $138,698 - $145,268 p.a., plus up to 17% employer superannuation Full-time, ongoing appointment The Opportunity UniSC is entering an exciting new chapter in how we deliver strategic outcomes across the University. As the scale, complexity and importance of our initiatives continue to grow, the newly established Enterprise Portfolio and Delivery Office (EPDO) will play a central role in strengthening how strategic initiatives are prioritised, governed and delivered across the University. The Office provides a coordinated, university-wide approach to portfolio governance, delivery management, organisational change, assurance and benefits realisation, helping ensure our most important investments achieve their intended outcomes. We are seeking an experienced and influential change professional to join this new capability as Manager, Organisational Change and Benefits Realisation. Reporting to the Director, Enterprise Portfolio and Delivery, you will lead the development and continuous improvement of UniSC's organisational change and benefits realisation capability. Working across a diverse portfolio of strategic initiatives, you will strengthen how the University approaches change, adoption, business readiness and benefits realisation, ensuring investments translate into meaningful and sustainable outcomes. Working closely with business leaders, project teams, sponsors and governance stakeholders, you will help embed consistent change and benefits practices across the University's strategic portfolio, providing visibility of organisational impacts, adoption risks and realised value. This is a unique opportunity to influence how UniSC navigates change and help shape a capability that will support the University's future direction. Why this role? Projects only create value when people adopt change and benefits are realised. As Manager, Organisational Change and Benefits Realisation, you will help shape how UniSC supports people through change and ensures strategic investments deliver meaningful and sustainable outcomes. You will lead the development of enterprise frameworks for change management and benefits realisation, influencing how initiatives are designed, adopted and embedded across the University. This is a unique opportunity to create an enterprise-wide approach to change, providing insight into organisational readiness, change impacts, adoption risks and realised value across a growing strategic portfolio. For change professionals who are motivated by creating lasting organisational impact, this role offers the chance to establish a new capability, influence strategic decision-making and help ensure UniSC's future initiatives deliver benefits that endure long after implementation. You will lead and continuously enhance UniSC's organisational change and benefits realisation frameworks, ensuring a consistent approach across strategic initiatives; partner with business owners, sponsors and delivery teams to support successful adoption, business readiness and sustained organisational outcomes; embed change, adoption and benefits requirements into project delivery frameworks, governance eprocesses, assurance activities and business case development; provide professional guidance, coaching and quality assurance to change practitioners working across the portfolio to promote consistency and maturity of practice; develop an enterprise-wide view of change impacts and change saturation, providing insights that inform prioritisation, sequencing and delivery planning; advise leaders and sponsors on business readiness, adoption risk, stakeholder engagement, change quality and benefits realisation; and support the measurement of adoption, sustainment and realised benefits, using insights to strengthen portfolio performance and continuous improvement. About the Enterprise Portfolio and Delivery Office The Enterprise Portfolio and Delivery Office provides a University-wide capability for enterprise portfolio governance, intake and prioritisation, delivery confidence, change visibility and benefits realisation. The Office establishes a consistent enterprise framework for how organisational initiatives are assessed, prioritised, governed, assured, delivered, reported and transitioned into business operations. Operating through a federated delivery model, the Office supports business areas to deliver strategic initiatives while providing the frameworks, standards, assurance and portfolio visibility needed to improve institutional outcomes and maximise organisational value. About you You are an experienced organisational change professional who understands that successful delivery is about more than implementing projects. You know how to help people adopt change, build organisational readiness and ensure intended benefits are realised over time. You bring a track record of leading change and benefits initiatives within complex organisations and are comfortable navigating competing priorities, influencing senior stakeholders and translating strategy into practical, people-focused outcomes. You thrive in collaborative environments and are motivated by the opportunity to establish new ways of working that support lasting organisational success. You will possess: Relevant qualifications and substantial experience in organisational change management and benefits realisation, or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Experience leading change management and benefits realisation activities across complex programs, portfolios or enterprise-wide initiatives, including framework development and continuous improvement. Strong expertise in change impact assessment, stakeholder engagement, communications, business readiness, adoption, sustainment and benefits transition. Experience embedding change and benefits practices within project delivery lifecycles, governance standards, assurance processes and post-implementation reviews. Demonstrated ability to advise and influence senior stakeholders on change saturation, adoption risk, business readiness and benefits realisation. Experience working within complex federated or matrix environments, including providing practice leadership, coaching and guidance to change resources. Strong communication, facilitation, coaching, influencing and relationship management skills. The ability to translate strategic intent into practical adoption and benefits realisation outcomes while working collaboratively across governance, delivery and business teams. Don't meet every requirement? At UniSC, we understand that your work and life experiences can be just as valuable. If you're excited about this role but your CV doesn't align perfectly with our position description, we encourage you to apply anyway. You may be just the right candidate for this or one of our many other opportunities. UniSC is an equal opportunity employer, committed to diversity and inclusion. We encourage applications from all backgrounds, including those with disabilities, women in STEM, First Nations Peoples, and individuals of diverse cultures, genders, abilities, and experiences. We value achievement relative to opportunity and encourage your commentary on your achievements in this context. For additional support during the application process, please contact us at unisc-careers@usc.edu.au or call +61 7 5430 2830. How to apply Applications for this position close midnight, Sunday 27 September 2026 Position description: 494722 PD_Manager Organisational Change and Benefits Realisation.pdf Your completed application must include a resume and a statement of suitability (not to exceed two pages), which will be reviewed in alignment to the specified selection criteria as outlined within the position description. Further information regarding how to prepare your application is available on our website: Join our team. Have questions or want to know more? For a confidential discussion, please contact: Nico Bekker Director, Enterprise Portfolio Delivery Email: nbekker@usc.edu.au We would love the opportunity to get to know you better, but we know it works both ways. To get to know a little more about us, visit us at: Welcome to UniSC and LinkedIn Life UniSC values a diverse and talented workforce and invites applications from candidates who already have legal work rights in Australia. UniSC does not accept unsolicited applications. For agency inquiries, contact unisc-careers@usc.edu.au Discover UniSC We’re all about doing work that matters, connecting with great people, and being part of an incredible journey. While we’re not the largest university, we are one of the fastest growing in Australia, now with over 2,000 staff across five campuses in South East Queensland and an expanding presence in major capital cities, and we’re making a big impact every day through ground-breaking research, a strong commitment to sustainability, high-performance sport, and award-winning alumni. We are committed to delivering high-quality research and teaching that address major global and regional challenges, with established and emerging strengths in sustainability, environmental systems, biodiversity, aquaculture, preventative health and regional resilience. Our research excellence is internationally recognised through strong performance in global benchmarking, including leading rankings in the 2025 Times Higher Education (THE) Impact Rankings for “Zero Hunger,” “Climate Action” and “Life on Land.” UniSC is also recognised for its teaching excellence, with a strong emphasis on student success, innovative and engaging learning experiences, and strong graduate outcomes that equip learners to make meaningful contributions in their chosen fields. As the only university operating within three UNESCO Biosphere Reserves and a UNESCO World Heritage Site, UniSC is uniquely positioned to leverage its natural environment to advance impactful research, teaching and partnerships that support sustainable futures, with sustainability embedded across all aspects of our teaching, research and operations. We foster a collaborative and supportive environment that encourages continuous professional development and provides the tools and resources to grow your career. We value the contributions of every team member and the role they play in our culture and success. We’re not afraid to do things differently, and we’re looking for people who share our values and want to be part of a team working together to make a meaningful difference to local and global challenges. Our Culture & Benefits: Our collaborative, passionate and welcoming culture is what really sets us apart. Modern teaching & research facilities. Professional development and career pathway opportunities. We are a proud recipient of the prestigious Athena SWAN Bronze Award, granted as part of the Science in Australia Gender Equity (SAGE) initiative. Flexible work arrangements & generous leave options. Salary packing options + 17% Super. EAP, fitness passport & discounted private health. < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNTIES Apply now! Enter your details below to commence your application: First Name (required) 01d63ab4 Last Name (required) 700c124b Email (required) 87d53221 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you About UniSC For more information about UniSC's employment benefits and culture, including employee blogs, visit our employer information page . Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 3:17 Loaded : 0% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 3:17 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles subtitles settings , opens subtitles settings dialog subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. Recommended for you Clinical Trial Associate UniSC SouthBank Clinical Trials, Individual contributor, L5 $82,843 - $93,358 +17% super, Professional Join UniSC's SouthBank clinic to support compliant, high-quality research, ensuring ethical protocols, Good Clinical Practice standards, and impactful outcomes are met. Administration Officer (Program Support) UniSC Sunshine Coast Academic Support Unit, Administration / Admin Support, L5 $82,843 - $93,358 +17% super Join UniSC and play an important role in supporting high-quality learning and research experiences for Honours and HDR students. Senior Clinical Trial Coordinator UniSC Sunshine Coast Clinical Trials, Individual contributor, L7 $105,843 - $115,703 +17% super, Nursing, Professional Join UniSC and lead clinical trial teams to deliver high-quality, ICH/GCP-compliant research, using expert coordination, problem-solving and innovative approaches to drive successful trial outcomes. Change Manager - Timetabling UniSC Sunshine Coast Individual contributor, Information Technology, L8 $118,986 - $134,756 +17% super Join UniSC’s PACE transformation and lead organisational change for a major evolution of the University’s timetabling and learning and teaching environment, helping staff and stakeholders successfully navigate and embrace new ways of working. Join our talent community! Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 1367bc88 Last Name (required) b6b8c151 Email (required) 895cdd38 Job Alert 8e462b73 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Enterprise Portfolio and Delivery Office L9 $138,698 - $145,268 +17% super Professional Enterprise Portfolio and Delivery Office L9 $138,698 - $145,268 +17% super Professional Employment Type Full-Time Full-Time Locations UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia Send Please wait... Done Not You? Congratulations from the UniSC Talent Acquisition Team, you are now signed up for UniSC job alerts. Apply now! Enter your details below to commence your application: First Name (required) bb02d5b5 Last Name (required) 3aa54fbb Email (required) d164ec44 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 3:17 Loaded : 0% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 3:17 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles subtitles settings , opens subtitles settings dialog subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is