    "https://careers.usc.edu.au/jobs/senior-infrastructure-engineer-unisc-sunshine-coast-qld-australia": {
      "title": "Senior Infrastructure Engineer",
      "description": "Senior Infrastructure Engineer - UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia Contact Us Candidate login Explore Opportunities Academic jobs Professional jobs Casual jobs Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander jobs Recruitment process Employer information Applicant Settings Kiosk mode < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNITIES Senior Infrastructure Engineer 90 Sippy Downs Drive, UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia, 4556 Individual contributor Information Technology L8 $118,986 - $134,756 +17% super Full-Time Add to favourites View favourites Information Technology Services |UniSC Sunshine Coast, Sippy Downs Level 8, $118,986 - $134,756 p.a., plus up to 17% employer superannuation Full-time (36.25 hrs per week), fixed term appointment for 12 months The Opportunity UniSC's Information Technology team is a strategic partner in delivering innovative, reliable and secure technology services that support teaching, learning, research and business operations. As the University continues its digital transformation journey, Enterprise Services plays a critical role in modernising network services, enhancing cyber resilience and delivering a secure, high-performing digital campus experience. As the Senior Infrastructure Engineer (Network Services), you will provide technical leadership across UniSC's enterprise network environment, spanning campus, data centre, cloud and wide area networking technologies. Working closely with stakeholders, project teams, vendors and service providers, you will guide network architecture decisions, develop strategic roadmaps and ensure the delivery of secure, scalable and resilient network services. You will play a key role in major network initiatives, including campus network modernisation, software-defined networking, wireless services, firewall platforms, internet connectivity and cloud networking. Through technical leadership, operational excellence and continuous improvement, you will help deliver future-ready network solutions that support the University's strategic objectives. For more information, please visit us online: Information Technology You will lead the design, implementation, support and continual improvement of UniSC's enterprise network environment, including campus networks, data centre networking, wireless services, SD-WAN, firewalls, load balancing and cloud connectivity; develop network architecture standards, technical roadmaps and strategic plans that deliver secure, resilient, scalable and high-performing network services; provide expert technical leadership across network projects, including vendor evaluations, solution design reviews, implementation oversight, operational readiness and knowledge transfer activities; drive network automation, monitoring, operational excellence and service reliability through contemporary engineering practices, documentation and continuous improvement initiatives; provide advanced technical support and governance for complex network incidents, problems, changes and major service improvements; oversee work completed by external vendors and service providers, ensuring solutions align with UniSC standards, architecture principles and operational requirements; and contribute as a network subject matter expert to strategic University initiatives, supporting digital transformation, cybersecurity, cloud adoption and modern campus technology programs. About you You are an experienced infrastructure professional with a strong background in enterprise technologies, technical architecture and modern infrastructure operations. You enjoy solving complex technical challenges and have the ability to balance strategic thinking with hands-on delivery across diverse technology environments. A collaborative and trusted technical leader, you build strong relationships with stakeholders, communicate complex technical concepts clearly and thrive in environments undergoing digital transformation. You are passionate about continuous improvement and are motivated by delivering secure, reliable and innovative technology solutions that make a meaningful impact across the organisation. You will possess: postgraduate qualifications and/or extensive experience in network engineering, telecommunications, infrastructure engineering or an equivalent combination of relevant experience and expertise; extensive experience supporting complex enterprise network environments, including switching, routing, wireless networking, SD-WAN, firewalls, internet connectivity and cloud networking services; demonstrated experience developing network architectures, technical standards, roadmaps and strategic technology recommendations aligned with organisational objectives; experience implementing network automation and modern network management practices to improve service reliability, efficiency and operational outcomes; strong knowledge of network security principles, segmentation, access control, monitoring and resilience practices within enterprise environments; exceptional stakeholder engagement, communication and technical leadership skills, with the ability to influence architectural decisions and work effectively across technical and business teams; and proven experience leading complex network deployments, technology refreshes and service improvement initiatives within a large enterprise environment Don't meet every requirement? At UniSC, we understand that your work and life experiences can be just as valuable. If you're excited about this role but your CV doesn't align perfectly with our position description, we encourage you to apply anyway. You may be just the right candidate for this or one of our many other opportunities. UniSC is an equal opportunity employer, committed to diversity and inclusion. We encourage applications from all backgrounds, including those with disabilities, women in STEM, First Nations Peoples, and individuals of diverse cultures, genders, abilities, and experiences. We value achievement relative to opportunity and encourage your commentary on your achievements in this context. For additional support during the application process, please contact us at unisc-careers@usc.edu.au or call +61 7 5430 2830. Position Description: 494511_Senior Infrastructure Engineer.pdf How to apply UniSC values a diverse and talented workforce and invites applications from candidates who already have legal work rights in Australia. All applications must be lodged through our website. To apply please visit our website at: Careers at UniSC Applications for this position close midnight, Sunday 6 September 2026. Your completed application must include: a resume and a statement of suitability (not to exceed two pages), which be reviewed in alignment to the specified selection criteria as outlined within the position description. Further information regarding how to prepare your application is available on our website: Join our team UniSC does not accept unsolicited applications. For agency inquiries, contact unisc-careers@usc.edu.au We would love the opportunity to get to know you better, but we know it works both ways. To get to know a little more about us, visit us at : Welcome to UniSC and LinkedIn Life Have questions or want to know more? For a confidential discussion, please contact: Jason Parsons Manager, Data Integration & Digital Platforms - IT - Enterprise Services Telephone: 07 5430 2860 Email: jparsons@usc.edu.au Discover UniSC We're all about doing work that matters, connecting with great people, and being part of an incredible journey. We’re not the biggest university. But we’re growing every day, and doing big things. Like ground-breaking research, championing sustainability, producing gold-winning athletes and award-winning alumni. We're one of the fastest growing universities in Australia, growing to over 2,000 people across 5 campuses in South East Queensland and a growing footprint in major capital cities. Teaching excellence is at the heart of what we do, and our commitment to sustainability is integrated into our teaching, research, and daily operations. Our research tackles the most pressing challenges of our time, with 13 fields ranked well above world standard in the Excellence in Research for Australia (ERA) rankings, demonstrating outstanding performance across key disciplines. At UniSC, you will have the opportunity to make a meaningful impact on the educational landscape and contribute to shaping the future for generations to come. We foster a collaborative and supportive environment, encouraging continuous professional development and providing resources to enhance your career. We recognise and value the contributions of each team member to our culture and success. We're not afraid to be different, and we're looking for people who share our values and want to be part of a team that is working together to improve our local and global challenges. Our Culture & Benefits: Our collaborative, passionate and welcoming culture is what really sets us apart. Modern teaching & research facilities. Professional development and career pathway opportunities. We are a proud recipient of the prestigious Athena SWAN Bronze Award, granted as part of the Science in Australia Gender Equity (SAGE) initiative. Flexible work arrangements & generous leave options. Salary packing options + 17% Super. EAP, fitness passport & discounted private health. Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 0:00 Loaded : 0% Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 0:00 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles captions and subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opac